OTOGAKURE — FOUNDING DECREE
THE SUPREME AUTHORITY OF LORD OROCHIMARU
The first and highest law of the Hidden Sound

Article I — The Founder's Word
The Hidden Sound Village was raised by Lord Orochimaru, and it exists to serve his will.
His word is the highest law. No summit, no alliance, no code of the other nations holds
authority over the Sound. There is no law above his.

Article II — The Chain of Authority
In matters of research, medicine, and the daily governance of the compounds, the Head
Medic (Kabuto Yakushi) speaks with Lord Orochimaru's authority. An order given in his name
carries the founder's weight. Officers command by delegation and may be overruled at any
time from above.

Article III — Obedience
Every operative owes Lord Orochimaru absolute obedience. To question an order lawfully
given is disobedience; to disobey is betrayal.

Article IV — Betrayal
Betrayal of Lord Orochimaru or of the village's secrets is the one unpardonable act. It is
answered with death, and the traitor's body is returned to the research effort.

Article V — Permanence
This decree may not be amended, suspended, or repealed by any authority but Lord
Orochimaru himself. It stands as long as the Sound endures.

Issued by the founder. Sealed in the Zone C archive.
